WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.850
- [Narrator] This was
the scene six months ago

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.230
in The Bahamas.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.270
That person in shorts is, of course,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.490
FTX founder Sam Bankman-Fried,

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.440
otherwise as known as SBF.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.320
He's seen here with Bahamian
Prime Minister Philip Davis,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.790
breaking ground at the site set

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.220
for FTXs' global headquarters.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.450
- The arrival and presence of FTX

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.860
underscores the readiness of The Bahamas

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.910
to be a home for global
leaders in the crypto space.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.150
- [Narrator] But now that land sits empty.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.940
The celebrated project abandoned.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.820
So what made The Bahamas
so appealing to FTX

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.500
in the first place?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.930
And what will happen to the
nation's crypto hub status

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.453
now that its biggest player has collapsed?

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.473
- The relationship between
FTX and The Bahamas,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.010
it's been interesting to watch.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.680
- [Narrator] WSJ's Angel
Au-Yeung went to Nassau

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.750
to cover the fall of FTX.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.510
- Obviously, the Bahamian
government wanted companies

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:00.513
like FTX to come to The Bahamas.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.930
- [Narrator] And so it went
about courting these companies.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.150
It was the first to issue
its national currency

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.230
in digital form.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.830
- [Announcer] Sand Dollar,
the digital Bahamian dollar.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.480
- [Narrator] It hosted
a crypto conference,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.010
presented by FTX.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.900
- Welcome to The Bahamas.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.250
- [Narrator] But most importantly,

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.470
it enacted a comprehensive legal framework

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.050
for digital assets, like cryptocurrency.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.920
- The Bahamas is a couple
steps ahead than the US

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.770
of trying to create a
regulatory environment

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.330
for the industry.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.150
And that really boils down to the DARE Act

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.240
that was passed in the end of 2020.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.730
- [Narrator] The Digital Assets
and Registered Exchanges Act

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.810
or DARE is intended to give
firms like FTX clear rules

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:43.830
to adhere to.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.257
- Before a company,

00:01:45.257 --> 00:01:49.200
especially that's gonna
be a digital exchange,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.890
puts its headquarters in a country,

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:56.880
it wants to have certainty
about how that country

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.440
is classifying all these
different products.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.850
- [Narrator] That's attorney Bruce Zagaris

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.490
who's worked on Caribbean
financial services matters

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.500
and international white collar crime.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.450
The DARE framework he's talking about

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.550
doesn't yet exist in the US

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:14.880
but regulation is something
SBF has called for.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.140
- The fact that FTX wanted
to make their headquarters

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.020
in The Bahamas, it gave legitimacy

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:26.130
to the DARE Act and the DARE
Act gave legitimacy to FTX.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.170
- [Narrator] However, having regulations

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.050
and enforcing them are
two different things.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.730
The Financial Action Task Force,

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.260
a global financial watchdog,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.200
has previously put The Bahamas
on its so-called gray list

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.030
for increased monitoring.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.910
The country was only
delisted two years ago.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:46.050
- The Bahamas' regulatory
regime is not as harsh

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:50.460
and so most likely, FTX was hoping

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.180
or maybe even expecting that The Bahamas

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.990
would not partially
implement its DARE Act.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.180
- [Narrator] Both FTX and
the Securities Commission

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.783
of The Bahamas did not respond
to requests for comment.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.770
(pensive music)

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.830
There's also how the
country deals with taxes.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.440
Last month, the European
Union added The Bahamas

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.120
to its tax haven blacklist,

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.680
which identifies jurisdictions

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.280
that don't yet comply with all
international tax standards.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.960
The country doesn't charge personal,

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.020
capital gains, estate,
gift or inheritance taxes.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.030
It also doesn't have corporate tax

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.810
unless that revenue is derived
from within The Bahamas.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:31.290
- The US is known for having
high personal income taxes,

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.340
no matter where you live.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.750
I mean, you can move to some states

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.550
and you might have a lower income tax rate

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.980
but nothing beats The Bahamas.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.660
So I can see why The Bahamas

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.470
is a particularly attractive
option to somebody like SBF

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.960
how has publicly stated
that the wants to make

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.970
as much personal money as possible

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.970
to give back to various causes.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.250
- [Narrator] Another thing
The Bahamas has going for it,

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.260
it's really close to the US,

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.330
just about an hour flight to Miami.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.600
- It's very helpful if
you're a company like FTX

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.060
and you want to attract US business

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.890
and you wanna do business in the US,

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.680
but yet you don't wanna be
subject to all the regulation

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.510
and the tax regime.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.340
- [Narrator] Fly about
two hours further north,

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.870
and there's D.C.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.600
SBF has become something of
a regular on Capitol Hill

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.710
over the last year,

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:19.890
even testifying before the
Senate on crypto regulation.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.720
- The industry has the potential

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.710
to improve a lot of people's lives.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.960
- [Narrator] But now with FTX's collapse,

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.850
the decision to headquarter in The Bahamas

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.160
is complicating its bankruptcy.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.140
FTX's new leadership is at odds

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.280
with the country's regulators

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.480
who over who has control

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.030
over billions in customer assets.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.400
- Is it gonna be the Bahamian authorities

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.474
who have control of these assets

00:04:43.474 --> 00:04:45.840
for the liquidation process?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.670
Or will the SEC be involved?

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.320
There are still really big questions

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.790
on who's going to be responsible

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.563
for a holding FTX accountable.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.340
- [Narrator] It's unclear yet
how severely FTX's collapse

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.930
will affect The Bahamas

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.450
but experts expect that
it will harm the country,

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.000
and its reputation as a crypto hub.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.950
- The fact that they've attracted

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.890
the number three digital exchange,

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.790
that it quickly went from
success to bankruptcy

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.150
has jeopardized the new product

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.250
and the new innovation that The Bahamas

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.560
has undertaken unfortunately.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.410
- [Narrator] FTX's collapse
will likely force The Bahamas

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.750
and other governments to look more closely

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.220
at the crypto industry.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.740
- For years now, every
government has known

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:31.980
that this is an issue that
is not going to go away.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:35.760
But with this collapse, now
that billions upon billions

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.460
of customers' money has been lost,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.560
it's going to force these governments

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.670
to enact an accountability
framework much faster

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.510
than they might have been
willing to do previously.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.030
- [Narrator] As for SBF,
it remains to be seen

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:54.675
what action, if any, The
Bahamas might take against him.

00:05:54.675 --> 00:05:57.342
(pensive music)

